-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/08f4bf69-53e9-517a-baaa-5f4d90137462
-- title:
--   Ascent of regularity along a non-zero-divisor quotient
-- statement:
--   The module proves that regularity of a Noetherian local ring can be deduced from regularity of the quotient by a principal ideal generated by a non-zero-divisor in the maximal ideal, together with the generator-counting estimates it needs and explicit test cases.
--
--   The counting part works with Mathlib's `Submodule.spanFinrank`, the minimal cardinality of a generating set. For a surjective ring homomorphism $f : A \to B$, a finitely generated ideal $J \subseteq B$ and finitely generated $\ker f$, `spanFinrank_comap_le_of_surjective` bounds the minimal number of generators of $f^{-1}(J)$ by that of $J$ plus that of $\ker f$; the proof lifts a minimal generating set of $J$ through a section of $f$ and adjoins generators of the kernel. Specialising to local $A$, $B$ with $B$ Noetherian and $f$ surjective (so local), `spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_le_of_surjective` gives $\mu(\mathfrak m_A) \le \mu(\mathfrak m_B) + \mu(\ker f)$, and `finrank_cotangentSpace_le_of_surjective` restates this for Noetherian $A$, $B$ as an inequality between the residue-field dimensions of the cotangent spaces $\mathfrak m/\mathfrak m^2$, with the error term $\mu(\ker f)$.
--
--   The main result, `isRegularLocalRing_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient`, assumes $A$ Noetherian local, $x \in \mathfrak m_A$ a non-zero-divisor and $A/(x)$ regular, and concludes that $A$ is regular; it combines the bound $\mu(\mathfrak m_A) \le \mu(\mathfrak m_{A/(x)}) + 1$ with the dimension jump $\dim A/(x) + 1 = \dim A$ for a non-zero-divisor in the maximal ideal, and with the criterion that $\mu(\mathfrak m_A) \le \dim A$ suffices for regularity. A variant, `isRegularLocalRing_of_surjective_ker_span_singleton`, takes instead a surjection $f : A \to B$ with $\ker f = (x)$ and $B$ regular, transporting regularity along the induced isomorphism $A/(x) \cong B$.
--
--   Two families of auxiliary declarations exhibit the scope of the statement. For a prime $p$, `padicIntQuotientSpanPEquiv` is the isomorphism $\mathbb Z_p/(p) \cong \mathbb Z/p$, and the accompanying results verify the three hypotheses for $A = \mathbb Z_p$, $x = p$, deduce that $\mathbb Z_p$ is a regular local ring, and record $\dim \mathbb Z_p/(p) + 1 = \dim \mathbb Z_p$. For the dual numbers, `dualNumberFst` is the first-coordinate projection $K[\varepsilon] \to K$ as a ring homomorphism, with kernel $(\varepsilon)$ and induced isomorphism $K[\varepsilon]/(\varepsilon) \cong K$; over $\mathbb Q$ one gets that $\varepsilon$ lies in the maximal ideal, is nonzero, is not a non-zero-divisor (since $\varepsilon^2 = 0$), that $\mathbb Q[\varepsilon]/(\varepsilon)$ is regular while $\mathbb Q[\varepsilon]$ is not (its nilradical is maximal, so its Krull dimension is $0$ whereas $\mathfrak m \ne 0$), and hence `not_forall_isRegularLocalRing_of_quotient_dropping_nonZeroDivisor`: the universally quantified version of the ascent statement with the non-zero-divisor hypothesis deleted is false.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** Regular local rings (`IsRegularLocalRing`), minimal generator counts (`Submodule.spanFinrank`), cotangent spaces, Krull dimension and dual numbers (`DualNumber`, `TrivSqZeroExt`) are all Mathlib notions; this module adds the ascent of regularity along a quotient by a non-zero-divisor and the generator-counting inequalities for surjections, and packages `TrivSqZeroExt.fst` as a ring homomorphism.
--
--   **Where it is used.** Regularity of local rings such as $\mathbb{Z}_p$, and of local rings presented as quotients by a regular element, is part of the commutative-algebra background to the deformation-theoretic and patching arguments in the proof.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_AlgebraicGeometry_RegularLocalRingQuotientNonZeroDivisorAscent.lean

